data: {"type": "assistant", "id": "a2", "content": "Here's the draft. It's also in your Files as **Brewline AI Barista Response Post.md**.\n\n---\n\nBrewline launched an \"AI barista\" this week. It \"knows your taste better than you do\".\n\nI like that they're taking taste seriously. Most subscriptions don't.\n\nBut picking the right bag from twelve blends roasted weeks ago isn't the whole of taste. Freshness is. So is knowing who roasted it.\n\nLast month Ana, who roasts our Morning Ridge, changed the profile because the harvest came in brighter. Nobody asked her to. That's the part of taste an algorithm can't pick for you.\n\nA subscription should get you closer to the people who make your coffee, not further away.\n\n---\n\nIt stays fair to Brewline, uses one concrete story (Ana and Morning Ridge), and keeps the close short."}

