data: {"type": "assistant", "id": "a5", "content": "Fixed. Updated post:\n\n---\n\nSaw Brewline's launch this morning. An \"AI barista\" that knows your taste better than you do.\n\nHonestly? Good on them for caring about taste. Plenty of subscriptions just send the same bag forever.\n\nBut I keep thinking about Ana. She roasts our Morning Ridge, and last month she changed the profile because the harvest came in brighter than last year. Nobody asked her to. She tasted it and knew.\n\nAn algorithm can choose a bag. It can't tell you it was roasted on Tuesday. I'd rather know who roasted mine, and when.\n\nMaybe that's old-fashioned. I don't think it is.\n\n---\n\nThe contrast is now about roast date, not about Brewline's catalog."}

